From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmd: ~s shortens the last name of a path that exists, too

%~si and %~fsi shortened only the folder part and kept the last name as it
was written. So the short form of "C:\Program Files\QGIS 3.44.15" was
"C:\PROG~FBU\QGIS 3.44.15", and the space in the last name stayed.
OSGeo4W's o4w_env.bat takes its root that way and then runs
  for %%f in ("%OSGEO4W_ROOT%\etc\ini\*.bat") do call "%%f"
With a space in the root, that called nothing, so QGIS 3.44 started without
Qt on its PATH ("Could not load qgis_app.dll"). Now a path that exists is
shortened whole, as cmd does on Windows. A name that does not exist still
follows its shortened folder as written.

--- a/programs/cmd/batch.c
+++ b/programs/cmd/batch.c
@@ -509,6 +509,15 @@
       /* Convert fullfilename's path to a short path - Save filename away as
          only path is valid, name may not exist which causes GetShortPathName
          to fail if it is provided                                            */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_TILDE_S_LONG_NAME
+      /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 8418): a name that exists is shortened too, as cmd does:
+       * %~fsi of "C:\Program Files\QGIS 3.44.15" kept "QGIS 3.44.15" whole, and OSGeo4W's
+       * o4w_env.bat then could not call its "etc\ini\*.bat" (QGIS: qgis_app.dll not found) */
+      if (exists && GetShortPathNameW(fullfilename, thisoutput, MAX_PATH)
+          && wcslen(thisoutput) < ARRAY_SIZE(fullfilename)) {
+        lstrcpyW(fullfilename, thisoutput);
+      } else
+#endif
       if (filepart) {
         lstrcpyW(thisoutput, filepart);
         *filepart = 0x00;
